MEMORY

Work from one session is gone next session unless remembered.
- memory/remember
- memory/recall
- memories
- memory/forget
- memory/forget-all
- memory/replay
- memory/revise
- memory/areas
- memory/builtins
- memory/list
Remember a wrong guess the moment it fails. Recall before you guess.
Fires by itself with :when "situation" [:unless "situation"], recognized by meaning before every step, or :on (kind pattern) for an exact event: call, result, error, step, prose, user, recall, start.
Signatures, examples, rules: memory/recall "memory/writing", or its trigger.

CHAINING
:links ("key" ...) loads listed memories along with this one: (memory "browser/local" :when "agent is about to automate a web browser" :links ("browser/flags")). Memories firing in same step get wired together too.
Start memory: trigger (start), rides user's first message. Put role and goal there. Loads once; revision read only by next conversation.
Fired memory is REPL feedback to you alone: not run, user cannot see it. To run it, memory/replay.
Built-in loads once, stays while its text is in context, loads again only after text leaves. Need one now? Recall by key or words.
